      ":question/id": "807c1c95-6fea-5d65-a59b-b497c894ecc9",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-119947",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify $$\n\\displaystyle {\\left(\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\right)}^{2}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we expand the parenthesis and use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\right)}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)+2\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)+{cos}^{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left[{sin}^{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)+{cos}^{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\right]+2\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =1+2\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x=\\operatorname{sin}2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\left(\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\right)}^{2}=1+2\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)=1+\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right).\n$$"
    },
    {
