      ":question/id": "984868e6-9b0d-5753-97a4-a56b885226b2",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-119948",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ into the above, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)}=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
