      ":question/id": "71319f17-956d-5226-b02f-5e0082742e93",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-7675",
      ":question/problem": "Express $$\n\\displaystyle 8\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)\n$$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{2\\pi }{5}\\right).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n8\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)=4\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)=4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{2\\pi }{5}\\right).\n$$"
    },
